---
title: Chilled Spanish Gazpacho
servings: 6
course: Starter
locale: en
difficulty: medium
cuisine: Spanish
---

= Soup =

Begin by placing the @tomatoes{700%g}(firm red ripe) in a bowl and pouring boiling water over them; after a minute or two the skins will loosen and slip off very easily. Halve the tomatoes, scoop out and discard the seeds and roughly chop the flesh.

Now place the tomatoes, @cucumber{10%cm}(peeled and chopped), @spring onions{3}(peeled and chopped), @garlic{2%cloves}(peeled and crushed), and @red or green pepper{0.5}(deseeded and chopped) in a liquidiser, adding a seasoning of @salt and @black pepper{}(freshly ground), the @basil, marjoram, or thyme{1%tsp}, @olive oil{4%tbsp}, and @wine vinegar{1.5%tbsp}. Then blend everything at top speed until the soup is absolutely smooth. Taste to check the seasoning and pour the soup into a bowl. Stir in a little @cold water{200%ml} to thin it slightly, then cover the bowl with foil and chill thoroughly.

= Garnish =

Combine the @red or green pepper{0.5}(deseeded and very finely chopped), @cucumber{10%cm}(peeled and finely chopped), @spring onions{2}(finely chopped), @egg{1}(hard boiled and finely chopped), and @parsley{1%tbsp}(fresh chopped) together with a seasoning of @salt and @black pepper{}(freshly ground). Fry @bread{}(small cubes) in @olive oil{} until crisp, then drain and allow to cool.

Serve the soup with @ice cubes{4} floating in it, together with the garnish and croutons.